  "design": {
    "family_theme": "Original mythical keeper of patterned-fen memory: three broad peat-rib limbs cradle a small spirit with an exposed pale face and a three-petal lavender island hood. One leaf-like arm opens low and outward while another curves behind the hood; two open fen-pool gaps separate the ribs. It reads a past season from each layer and can fold one forgotten path into another. The name refers to flark pools, not an existing sacred spirit. Its spectral recollections and path-folding are an original Ghost/Fairy enchantment.",
